                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237601409",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561199071580532",
                            "num_reviews": 31,
                            "playtime_forever": 337,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 337,
                            "last_played": 1791166037
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This CoD is by far my favorite game and it is softly because of nostalgia. In seriousness though, the story and gameplay is what you can expect from any previous CoD that came before this one. The only reason this game isn't talked about as much was because the multiplayer wasn't as good as previous entries and that is the sole reason this game wasn't popular that and maybe it didn't have zombies. Those two things during the time it came out was arguably at it's highest gaming peak, so it makes sense it didn't get as much attention. Which is a damn shame because this has one of the coolest story moments for your squad: the Ghosts. Plus, it also introduces a different game mode extinction where you take out aliens and set up defenses which was an attempt at a different style over zombies. I think it was really cool and a unique concept though I think what dragged that down was there was only 1-2 maps to actually play it on, so it got really repetitive and stale the older the game got. Instead of remastering and making terrible new entries how about actually following up the story on this one? It has some clunk to it, but I honestly think that is because it is just an older game now. Give this entry a shot because it is my all-time sleeper pick that I would recommend anyone 10/10!",
                        "timestamp_created": 1791860745,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1791860745,
